{"nodes": [{"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_md", "label": "09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "You cannot hold a transaction open across a client round trip, and there are three independent reasons rather than one \u2014 the manual advises against it, the platform may freeze the function that opened it, and behind a pooler the next statement will not reach the same backend anyway", "sidebar_label": "09e \u00b7 Transactions and the HTTP boundary", "sidebar_position": "50", "description": "The three mechanisms that each independently forbid a request-spanning transaction, why this is the reason optimistic concurrency exists, the application-level lease that gives you what people actually want, and the idle_in_transaction timeout that limits the damage."}}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_reason_1_the_manual_tells_you_not_to_and_the_mechanism_is_unbounded_waiting", "label": "Reason 1 \u2014 the manual tells you not to, and the mechanism is unbounded waiting", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L16"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_reason_2_the_function_that_opened_it_may_not_be_there_when_you_want_to_close_it", "label": "Reason 2 \u2014 the function that opened it may not be there when you want to close it", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L28"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_reason_3_behind_a_pooler_the_next_statement_is_not_on_the_same_backend", "label": "Reason 3 \u2014 behind a pooler, the next statement is not on the same backend", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L40"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_therefore_the_token_not_the_lock", "label": "Therefore: the token, not the lock", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L67"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_what_people_actually_want_a_lease", "label": "What people actually want: a lease", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L85"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_limiting_the_damage_from_the_ones_that_slip_through", "label": "Limiting the damage from the ones that slip through", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/09e-a-transaction-cannot-span-an-http-boundary.md", "source_location": "L133"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_09e_a_transaction_cannot_span_an_http_boundary_gotchas", "label": "Gotchas